Pre-note criteria (recorded before opening docs/design/std-3.md)

Controlling sources: spec (especially 4.1, 4.5-4.8, 6.2, 9.6, 9.10, 10.2, 11, 13); accepted syntax; std-1 pure-library, stream and cost contracts; runtime R1's exact SplitMix contract; literal-types and records compatibility; plan's STR interpolation and codepoint indexing scope. No library-specific inference, runner hooks, host math, keywords or hidden mutable state. New abstractions must be ordinary sets of values and useful in unrelated domains.

Property: define observable generator laws independently of closure identity. Fix random state consumption, size, range endpoints, empty choices, rejection limits, and dependent composition. Shrink candidates must preserve generator constraints; say what smaller means, ensure progress or explicitly bound traversal, and do not claim a global minimum from greedy traversal. Test mapped constant/non-monotone generators, bind dependencies, repeated/identity/cyclic shrink candidates, passing parent with failing descendants, infinite streams, and discard exhaustion. Replay must include sufficient versioned state (seed, case, size, shrink path, generator algorithm/config) and distinguish same-version determinism from cross-version compatibility. Assertions/errors/stops must follow 9.6/11.7; ordinary @test integration must really report failure without a special runner rule. Pure function types do not prove termination or determinism for identity-observing values.

Float: precise real function and rounding contract; distinguish approximation error from target reproducibility. Test neighbors of pi/2 and other quadrant boundaries, maximum finite and huge powers, tiny normal/subnormal inputs/results, positive/negative zero, inverse endpoints and out-of-domain arguments, atan2 zero quadrants and extreme ratios, hypot scaling/overflow and exact ties, angle overflow/underflow. NaN/infinity cannot enter Float: reject at boundary, never construct an intermediate nonfinite value. Interval refinement must enclose exact values with outward rounding, resolve cancellation, terminate even at exact binary64 midpoints, and round once without double rounding. Independently calculate high-precision results and measure representative plain-i bigint work. Compare a deterministic bounded-error algorithm with correct rounding, respecting section 11 and the existing float module's contracts.

String: inventory all exports to exclude semantic duplicates. Check each added operation on empty, multibyte, combining-mark and supplementary codepoints; negative and huge indexes; start/end versus length; clipping versus error; empty needle/separator/padding and overlapping matches. Keep offsets codepoints and make O(bytes), allocation and repeated-use costs honest. Do not imply grapheme indexing, Unicode normalization or constant-time access. New helpers must not preempt STR interpolation/string patterns or change source literal semantics.

Evidence: code references must exist and support claims; proposed unimplemented APIs require executable models or clearly labeled inference. Each finding needs a concrete counterexample and a material consequence, plus a simpler repair and evidence that could overturn it. Record no stylistic preferences as defects.
